// policy: semver arithmetic for M2's "version verdict" (Gate 2's roadmap:
// "M2 version verdict: policy incl. 0.x, --declared, --baseline <dir>,
// waivers, --explain, markdown for PR comments"). This round implements only
// the piece the owner chose to build first: `Version`, `required_version`
// (0.x-aware), `Verdict`, `verdict`. Pure -- depends on `compare` (for
// `Delta`/`Level`) and `moonbitlang/core/string` (for `parse_int`, used to
// parse a `Version` out of a plain "MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" string) but nothing
// else, same "no I/O" discipline `compare`/`report` already follow.
//
// Deliberately NOT implemented here (each is its own design pass, not
// guessed at under time pressure): `Waivers`/`Waivers::parse`/`Delta::apply`
// (no waiver file format is specified anywhere in Gate 1/2/3 -- inventing
// one needs its own decision, not a side effect of this step); `--baseline
// <dir>` whole-module comparison; `--explain`; `render_markdown`. See
// gate3-decisions-and-plan.md's M2 section.
//
// Wired into `src/cmd/mbti-compat`'s CLI as of the `--declared`/
// `--baseline-version` round: `--baseline <dir>` was already reserved (Gate
// 2 names it as a directory of `.mbti` files for a whole-module comparison,
// not a version number), so the invented flag for the *baseline*
// (currently-published) version `required_version`/`verdict` also need as
// an input is named `--baseline-version` instead, avoiding any collision
// with that still-unimplemented flag. See `src/cmd/mbti-compat/main.mbt`'s
// `run_verdict` and gate3-decisions-and-plan.md's dedicated section on this.
import {
  "mbti-compat/src/compare",
  "moonbitlang/core/string",
}

// `ingest` is a test-only dependency: policy_wbtest.mbt's `patch_delta`/
// `minor_delta`/`major_delta` helpers need it to build a real `Delta` by
// running tiny `.mbti` source snippets through `@ingest.of_mbti_source(...)`
// + `@compare.compare(...)`, rather than hand-constructing `Delta`/`Change`
// struct literals directly (no precedent anywhere in this project does
// that -- see report_wbtest.mbt's own identical convention). The real
// `policy` package has no business depending on `ingest` itself.
import {
  "mbti-compat/src/ingest",
} for "wbtest"
